- And you walk around,
you see vending machines

00:51:32.910 --> 00:51:35.970
and Asuki and Mari and
Shinji is everywhere.

00:51:35.970 --> 00:51:38.850
- I really recommend, if
you want a nice kind of,

00:51:38.850 --> 00:51:42.570
maybe a two day trip outside of Tokyo,

00:51:42.570 --> 00:51:44.550
because Hakone is not only really good,

00:51:44.550 --> 00:51:46.170
especially if you love Eva, of course,

00:51:46.170 --> 00:51:49.710
but like also there's the Jigokudani,

00:51:49.710 --> 00:51:53.480
which is the sulfur plumes of
like the mountains of Hakone

00:51:53.480 --> 00:51:54.313
is really nice.

00:51:54.313 --> 00:51:55.620
- I've never been there before.

00:51:55.620 --> 00:51:56.453
- It's really dope.

00:51:56.453 --> 00:51:59.220
You go up this huge, I
was about to say monorail,

00:51:59.220 --> 00:52:01.260
it's not a monorail, it's like
a... what do they call it?

00:52:01.260 --> 00:52:04.140
Like this... fuck... what do they call it?

00:52:04.140 --> 00:52:06.960
It's like a, not a ski lift, but... what?

00:52:06.960 --> 00:52:08.670
- Gondola?
- Yeah. Gondola, that's it?

00:52:08.670 --> 00:52:10.050
Yeah, you go up this gondola

00:52:10.050 --> 00:52:13.840
from the base of this lake in Hakone,

00:52:13.840 --> 00:52:15.600
and you go up into the mountains

00:52:15.600 --> 00:52:17.610
and you get this really,
really nice view of the lake

00:52:17.610 --> 00:52:19.620
and on a good day, if the
weather's really good,

00:52:19.620 --> 00:52:21.950
you can see this perfect
view of Mount Fuji as well.

00:52:21.950 --> 00:52:23.220
So that's really dope.

00:52:23.220 --> 00:52:25.590
And then you go into this little valley

00:52:25.590 --> 00:52:27.120
and you go into this
place called Jigokudani,

00:52:27.120 --> 00:52:28.622
which is called Hell's Valley.

00:52:28.622 --> 00:52:30.308
Japan has a couple of Hell's Valleys.

00:52:30.308 --> 00:52:31.560
- Oh I know. Yeah.

00:52:31.560 --> 00:52:32.659
Isn't there one in Hokkaido, as well?

00:52:32.659 --> 00:52:34.185
- There's one in Hokkaido as well.

00:52:34.185 --> 00:52:36.240
And there's also one
around like Gifu as well.

00:52:36.240 --> 00:52:40.860
But, yeah, it's just this
really cool sulfur plume place

00:52:40.860 --> 00:52:43.590
where you can get really close
to volcanic sulfur plumes.

00:52:43.590 --> 00:52:46.160
It kind of smells like
farts the entire time.

00:52:46.160 --> 00:52:47.320
- Sulfur does like farts.

00:52:47.320 --> 00:52:50.994
- But it's kind of a really
cool, unique experience.

00:52:50.994 --> 00:52:52.183
Yeah, I personally recommend it.

00:52:52.183 --> 00:52:53.016
It's a good day trip.

00:52:53.016 --> 00:52:53.849
- Yeah, because I really,

00:52:53.849 --> 00:52:57.117
Hakone was the first hot
springs town that I went to

00:52:57.117 --> 00:52:58.860
and I really enjoyed myself.

00:52:58.860 --> 00:53:02.332
The one thing I will say
is, if you go to Hakone,

00:53:02.332 --> 00:53:06.180
it's really weird,
because I went to Hakone,

00:53:06.180 --> 00:53:09.510
and I expected it to be
something, not similar to Tokyo,

00:53:09.510 --> 00:53:11.640
but you expect to go to a hot spring

00:53:11.640 --> 00:53:13.860
and then you expect to walk
around and explore somewhere,

00:53:13.860 --> 00:53:16.380
but a lot of ryokans,

00:53:16.380 --> 00:53:19.620
they expect you to stay
at that one establishment

00:53:19.620 --> 00:53:21.751
for the entirety of your trip, right?

00:53:21.751 --> 00:53:24.960
A lot of these hotels, and
a lot of these ryokans,

00:53:24.960 --> 00:53:29.960
will have everything you
need within that facility

00:53:30.630 --> 00:53:33.270
because they don't really expect
you to go out and explore,

00:53:33.270 --> 00:53:35.640
because normally there
isn't really much to explore

00:53:35.640 --> 00:53:38.490
in that immediate area, unless
you take a bus or something,

00:53:38.490 --> 00:53:39.330
right.
- Yeah.

00:53:39.330 --> 00:53:40.711
- At least that's my experience.

00:53:40.711 --> 00:53:43.020
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- So don't expect...

00:53:43.020 --> 00:53:45.480
Like, you can go explore, but
if you want to go explore,

00:53:45.480 --> 00:53:47.580
you probably need to
plan it out a bit more

00:53:47.580 --> 00:53:49.570
because the place you're staying in

00:53:50.580 --> 00:53:53.040
isn't necessarily going to be near

00:53:53.040 --> 00:53:55.200
a lot of tourist attractions.
- Yeah.

00:53:55.200 --> 00:53:57.810
- Especially if you're
staying at a ryokan.

00:53:57.810 --> 00:54:00.570
Having said that, if
you do stay in a ryokan,

00:54:00.570 --> 00:54:05.570
be prepared to get up and
eat fucking breakfast, okay.

00:54:05.878 --> 00:54:08.220
That's one thing which-

00:54:08.220 --> 00:54:10.380
- At an egregiously early time.

00:54:10.380 --> 00:54:12.720
- I'm not sure if I am a fan of it,

00:54:12.720 --> 00:54:14.573
but if you do stay in a ryokan,
ryokans are great, right.

00:54:14.573 --> 00:54:17.190
Ryokans are great, because I
feel like, in terms of hotels,

00:54:17.190 --> 00:54:19.290
they're like the most
aesthetic place you can stay.

00:54:19.290 --> 00:54:21.090
- Oh yeah.
- You are pampered there.

00:54:21.090 --> 00:54:22.200
It's great.

00:54:22.200 --> 00:54:25.380
- It's the most authentic
Japanese accommodation experience.

00:54:25.380 --> 00:54:28.074
- Yeah, exactly, and they
normally have the nicest onsens

00:54:28.074 --> 00:54:29.487
that you could find.

00:54:29.487 --> 00:54:31.923
- Oh, you normally sleep on a
futon, though, on the floor.

00:54:31.923 --> 00:54:34.860
So not a bed. So, if that's
something you might...

00:54:34.860 --> 00:54:36.690
- But if you want that
authentic Japanese experience.

00:54:36.690 --> 00:54:37.920
- Yeah, I like it. I like it.

00:54:37.920 --> 00:54:40.710
- Futons, I feel like, are
better than beds sometimes.

00:54:40.710 --> 00:54:42.280
- Yeah, but right,
people might not want to.

00:54:42.280 --> 00:54:43.350
- True.
- Some people might

00:54:43.350 --> 00:54:44.460
have a thousand thread count.

00:54:44.460 --> 00:54:47.052
- They might be thinking,
"Where's my bed,"

00:54:47.052 --> 00:54:48.875
when they get there.
- "There you are."

00:54:48.875 --> 00:54:49.708
"Is that it?"
- Yeah.

00:54:49.708 --> 00:54:51.700
But if you don't come down for
breakfast at the agreed time,

00:54:54.900 --> 00:54:56.100
they will find your family

00:54:56.100 --> 00:54:58.290
and they will kill everyone you love,

00:54:58.290 --> 00:55:00.119
or at least that's what I get out of-

00:55:00.119 --> 00:55:02.550
- It's included in the cost as well,

00:55:02.550 --> 00:55:04.110
so that's why they're
normally quite expensive,

00:55:04.110 --> 00:55:05.910
'cause dinner is normally included.

00:55:05.910 --> 00:55:07.830
- Yeah, they don't want you wasting money.

00:55:07.830 --> 00:55:08.910
- Yeah, yeah.
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:55:08.910 --> 00:55:11.850
I mean, these dinners are
normally really large courses,

00:55:11.850 --> 00:55:13.736
so they're the reason
why a ryokan seems...

00:55:13.736 --> 00:55:18.736
Ryokans are normally like
what, 3, $400 a night minimum,

00:55:18.743 --> 00:55:20.955
and that's 'cause half of
that has gone to the food,

00:55:20.955 --> 00:55:21.990
if not more.
- The food. Mm-hmm.

00:55:21.990 --> 00:55:23.460
- Yeah, you will be eating like a king.

00:55:23.460 --> 00:55:24.420
You will be eating like king.

00:55:24.420 --> 00:55:26.613
So if you see the price of the ryokan,

00:55:26.613 --> 00:55:28.080
don't get too shocked at the price,

00:55:28.080 --> 00:55:29.850
because you are paying
for the food as well,

00:55:29.850 --> 00:55:31.413
and it's normally
really, really good food.

00:55:31.413 --> 00:55:33.600
- High quality.
- It's high quality.

00:55:33.600 --> 00:55:35.940
It might be even a bit too much sometimes.

00:55:35.940 --> 00:55:38.760
- You'll get a good taste of
local dishes, though, normally.

00:55:38.760 --> 00:55:40.050
- Yeah.
- They use local ingredients.

00:55:40.050 --> 00:55:40.950
- Yep.
- And it's certainly

00:55:40.950 --> 00:55:42.930
a really good way to
just try Japanese food

00:55:42.930 --> 00:55:44.160
that you normally wouldn't order.

00:55:44.160 --> 00:55:45.990
Like, I'm never gonna order
half the shit they give me.

00:55:45.990 --> 00:55:47.850
- Oh yeah. Yeah.
- Because half of it

00:55:47.850 --> 00:55:49.290
is super slimy.
- Yeah.

00:55:49.290 --> 00:55:50.880
- But I'll always eat it,
because I don't want to

00:55:50.880 --> 00:55:52.890
